{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}Connect your assistant · MemorialAtlas{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<section style="max-width:860px">
<a href="{{ path('chat') }}">← Ask MemorialAtlas</a>
<h1>Connect your assistant</h1>
<p>Explore the collection from your own AI assistant. Search inscriptions, read proposed records, and follow links back to the photographs. No MemorialAtlas account is needed.</p>
{% include 'chat/_connect_instructions.html.twig' with {serverName: serverName, endpoint: endpoint} only %}
<h2>Try asking</h2>
<blockquote>Use MemorialAtlas to find stones that mention military service. Read the matching records, link to the photographs, and distinguish carved words from AI interpretations.</blockquote>
<h2>What the connector provides</h2>
<dl>
<dt><code>collection_overview</code></dt><dd>Collection coverage and processing counts.</dd>
<dt><code>search_memorials</code></dt><dd>Search names, inscriptions, descriptions, and symbols.</dd>
<dt><code>find_memorials</code></dt><dd>Find records by meaning using semantic search.</dd>
<dt><code>get_memorial</code></dt><dd>Read one record, its proposed people, uncertainties, and photo links.</dd>
<dt><code>collection_digest</code></dt><dd>Read summaries across the processed collection.</dd>
<dt><code>list_records_to_review</code></dt><dd>List records marked for review. This does not mean human review has taken place.</dd>
</dl>
<p>These are AI-generated readings, not verified burial records. The original photographs remain the evidence. A shared marker may name several people; a symbol does not necessarily describe every person named.</p>
<details><summary>Developers: use a local checkout</summary>
<p>For clients that support stdio, replace the path below with your checkout. The application must already be configured with access to its database and services.</p>
<pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "memorialatlas": {
      "command": "php",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/mematlas/bin/console", "mcp:server", "memorialatlas", "--no-debug", "--no-interaction"]
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
<p>No application provider keys need to be copied into your assistant. Semantic lookup uses the application’s configured embedding provider.</p>
</details>
</section>
{% endblock %}
